==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{m|non|orð}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{m|gem-pro|*wurdą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{m|ine-pro|*werdʰo-||word}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{m|ine-pro|*wer-||speak}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|word}}, {{cog|osx|word}}, {{cog|nl|woord}}, {{cog|goh|wort}} ({{cog|de|Wort}}), {{cog|sv|ord}}, {{cog|got|𐍅𐌰𐌿𐍂𐌳}}, and {{cog|en|word}}.

The Proto-Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|la|verbum}}, {{cog|lt|vardas}}, and, more distantly, of {{cog|grc|εἴρω||I say}} and {{cog|cu|ротити|ротити сѧ|to swear|sc=Cyrs}} ({{cog|ru|ротиться||to vow}}).

